.TH VIEWPORT 1 "August 2026" "viewport 0.1.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viewport \- a Wayland compositor whose shell is a web page
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viewport
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B viewport msg
.RI [ options ]
.B \-t
.IR type
.RI [ \-\-field " value" ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B viewport
is a Wayland compositor whose entire shell\(emwallpaper, dock, window frames,
titlebars\(emis a web page, composited zero\-copy alongside native Wayland
clients.  Smithay handles DRM/KMS, input and the xdg\-shell protocol; WebKit
renders the UI to a DMA\-BUF.
.PP
With no options it nests inside the session it was started from, which is what
trying it costs a window rather than the machine;
.B \-\-drm
takes the screens instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-drm
Take the screens and the seat: a session of its own, from a TTY.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
No renderer and no window: everything but drawing, for tests.
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N"
The headless output's width (default 1920).
.TP
.BI \-\-height " N"
And its height (default 1080).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
The config file, instead of the default one.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " NAME"
.BR tiling ,
.BR scrolling ,
.BR solar ,
.B matrix
or
.BR canvas ,
over whatever the config says.
.TP
.BI \-\-renderer " NAME"
Vulkan or gles, over $VIEWPORT_RENDERER.
.TP
.BI \-\-pixel-format " N"
Scanout bits per channel:
.BR 8 ,
.B 10
or
.BR auto ,
over $VIEWPORT_PIXEL_FORMAT and the config file's
.BR pixel_format .
.TP
.BI \-\-shell-backend " NAME"
Which engine draws the desktop; see
.IR docs/shell-backends.md .
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
A page to run instead of the bundled desktop.
.TP
.B \-\-url\-span
Give that page every monitor, not just the first.
.TP
.B \-\-watch\-shell
Reload the shell when its files change.
.TP
.B \-\-watch\-config
Reload the configuration file when it changes.
.TP
.BI \-\-background-terminal " [CMD]"
A terminal for a wallpaper, running CMD if one is given.
.TP
.BI \-\-wallpaper " PATH"
The desktop background, over the config file's
.BR wallpaper .
A path or a URL for a picture, or a CSS value for a colour or a gradient
.RB ( #1a1b26 ", " "rgb(...)" ", " "linear-gradient(...)" ).
.TP
.BI \-\-wallpaper-mode " NAME"
How a picture is fitted to the screen:
.BR fill ", " fit ", " stretch ", " center " or " tile
.RB ( fill
by default). The names stylix's
.B imageScalingMode
uses.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
The control socket, instead of the one named after the display.
.TP
.BI \-\-exit-after " SECS"
Stop after this long, in case stopping is what is broken.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this help and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B msg
Drive a running compositor over its control socket.
.B "viewport msg \-\-help"
lists every message.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIEWPORT_LOG
An env_logger filter that controls log verbosity (default
.BR info ).
Set
.B VIEWPORT_LOG=debug
for everything the shell says.
.TP
.B VIEWPORT_RENDERER
The renderer to use (vulkan or gles); overridden by
.BR \-\-renderer .
.TP
.B VIEWPORT_PIXEL_FORMAT
Scanout bits per channel (8, 10 or auto); overridden by
.BR \-\-pixel-format ,
and itself overriding the config file.
.TP
.B VIEWPORT_SHELL_BACKEND
Which engine draws the shell; overridden by
.BR \-\-shell-backend .
.TP
.B VIEWPORT_PAM_SERVICE
Which PAM service the built-in lock screen authenticates against.  Absent, it
is
.B viewport
where
.I /etc/pam.d/viewport
exists and
.B login
otherwise.  Only consulted when
.B idle.lock_command
is unset, since a configured locker checks the password itself.
.TP
.B VIEWPORT_SOCKET
The control socket
.B viewport msg
uses when neither
.B \-\-socket
nor the default path applies.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/viewport/config.json
The configuration file.  The reference material lives in
.IR docs/configuration.md .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.nf
viewport                        # nest in this session
viewport \-\-drm                 # take the screens, from a TTY
viewport \-\-url http://localhost:3000   # run a page instead of the desktop
viewport msg \-t view.focus \-\-id 12     # focus a window by id
viewport msg \-t output.query \-\-pretty  # list outputs
viewport msg \-t subscribe view.focused  # follow events until ^C
viewport msg \-t quit            # from a second TTY
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docs/configuration.md ,
.BR docs/ipc.md ,
.BR docs/shell-backends.md ,
.BR docs/protocols.md .
